    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# AI Social Media Content & Instagram Publishing Automation\n\n## What this workflow does\nRuns daily, generates an Instagram content idea, writes a caption, creates 20 hashtags, generates a post image, saves the content plan to Google Sheets, and publishes the post to Instagram.\n\n## Required setup\n1. Connect the buyer's own OpenAI credential in the AI nodes.\n2. Install/configure the Instagram publishing community node used by this workflow.\n3. Connect Google Sheets and Google Drive credentials.\n4. Create a Google Sheet for the content planner.\n5. Set `CONTENT_PLANNER_SHEET_ID`.\n6. Set `INSTAGRAM_BUSINESS_ACCOUNT_ID`.\n7. Optional: set `INSTAGRAM_IMAGE_FOLDER_ID`.\n8. Confirm the n8n timezone because the schedule uses 9:00 AM in the n8n instance timezone.\n\n## Sheet columns\nTopic | Caption | Hashtags | Status | PublishDate | ImageURL (optional)\n\n## Important\nWorkflow is inactive by default. Test it manually before enabling the schedule.",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 480
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1320,
        -1760
      ],
      "id": "1dff7112-842e-4476-b8d4-ec2475d6a34d",
      "name": "NOTES • Buyer Setup Guide"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Customize Before Deployment\n\nEdit `Config • Content Settings`:\n\n- **Niche** — e.g. Real Estate, Fitness, SaaS, Coaching\n- **TargetAudience** — who the content is for\n- **Platform** — currently Instagram\n- **ContentPillar** — topics the brand should publish\n- **BrandTone** — professional, friendly, educational, bold, etc.\n- **ContentFormat** — educational, promotional, tips, case study, etc.\n\n## Publishing note\nThis is an Instagram-focused workflow. Do not market it as multi-platform unless additional publishing integrations are added and tested.\n\nThe Instagram node receives a publicly accessible Google Drive image URL. Test that Instagram can fetch the image before enabling automatic publishing.\n\n## AI output note\nThe AI agents are instructed to return JSON. The workflow also safely extracts the JSON fields before saving/publishing so raw JSON is not unintentionally posted as the caption.",
        "height": 570,
        "width": 480
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2820,
        -1760
      ],
      "id": "9205d445-d759-4ab2-8ee5-d10cb784eea3",
      "name": "NOTES • Customization & Publishing"
    }
